                        ],
                        "form": "pansexuels"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "7ea708be-2b24-4792-8d50-05b55bc693db",
                        "entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "pansexuelle"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "688fa459-0348-4db0-b9d3-c676dfd7367c",
                        "entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "pansexuelles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                        "entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie une personne qui est attirée, sexuellement ou sentimentalement, par une autre personne sans considération de son genre, identité de genre ou sexe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b29b5192-4782-4095-bfc4-fa38a86b8d46",
                                "sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                                "text": "C’est une farandole qui gonfle mon journal et trouble ma petite âme (immortelle), le petit lac pur de ma conscience que fait doucement moutonner la brise rougissante des chastes émois pan-sexuels."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02080748-f0bd-4754-b0f4-0ca97257cf4a",
                                "sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                                "text": "Un nombre croissant d'ados refusent l'idée d'être homo ou hétéro, mais explorent des degrés de bisexualité. Un nouveau monde de nuances émerge, ou l'on peut se découvrir neutre, pansexuel, cisgenré, transgenre, demisexuel, grissexuel, aromantique, gynesexuel ou genderfluid..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdfb4350-4815-4806-b165-21d8d518d624",
                                "sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                                "text": "Au début du collège, j’avais des amoureux garçons, et des très très très bonnes amies filles, explique Jacquie. Je me suis d’abord définie comme bisexuelle, puis pansexuelle qui est plus inclusif, puis queer, un terme générique pour dire qu’on n’est pas dans la binarité, parce que j’en avais marre d’utiliser dix mots différents !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94e8a18d-879e-4e54-859a-deb645400bb2",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                        "target_lang_word": "pansexual",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pansexual",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8251a244-e34e-3464-9797-6b178eb05b05",
                                        "entry_id": "c3d90f71-9850-3d6f-aee7-3bf1e13fd1de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexually attracted to people regardless of gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01e77014-8e30-4354-be02-7391ea6b3ff5",
                                                "sense_id": "8251a244-e34e-3464-9797-6b178eb05b05",
                                                "text": "Karen and Carlos are definitely pansexual people who have paired off to have this child, and this seems real and good to them now. When I had been with Karen, she had floated through several gay relationships, […] all my friends had been what I would call pansexual, avoiding the older term bisexual, which is meaningless when you can count more than two sexes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "072f8c31-855b-44e7-8a86-f5dbf43e49ba",
                                                "sense_id": "8251a244-e34e-3464-9797-6b178eb05b05",
                                                "text": "Obviously many women who answered the survey considered themselves bisexual in the past no longer do. Perceiving oneself as bisexual was often a stage of transition between heterosexuality and homosexuality. But others did consider and still consider themselves bisexual. Here are some stories of bisexual or pansexual women and some comments about [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50d02acc-9243-4f90-99e4-7ee61717683e",
                                                "sense_id": "8251a244-e34e-3464-9797-6b178eb05b05",
                                                "text": "As a writer/sexologist, he argues that people are neither homosexual nor heterosexual but pansexual."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64629f75-2f04-48ee-8a46-43d042773154",
                                                "sense_id": "8251a244-e34e-3464-9797-6b178eb05b05",
                                                "text": "CUMMING: Bisexual, I suppose... No, pansexual. Some bloke in a newspaper called me a \"frolicky pansexual sex symbol for the new millennium.\" I thought that was fabulous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76b1d3e2-7e93-3ea2-bbb6-2a2bc3ea4c2e",
                                        "entry_id": "c3d90f71-9850-3d6f-aee7-3bf1e13fd1de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexually attracted to everyone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb3910f6-f254-4a3a-b436-baa0ea0d097f",
                                                "sense_id": "76b1d3e2-7e93-3ea2-bbb6-2a2bc3ea4c2e",
                                                "text": "To the end he [Walt Whitman] denied that he was homosexual; his writings are pansexual, finding carnal ripeness in the soul, in nature, as well as in men and women."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "971ac40b-5ad7-362e-aff4-3ee9e1076f96",
                                        "entry_id": "c3d90f71-9850-3d6f-aee7-3bf1e13fd1de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Welcoming people of all sexual orientations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90647cd3-d2d9-4bca-9b32-b2e58b487ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "971ac40b-5ad7-362e-aff4-3ee9e1076f96",
                                                "text": "We like to attend pansexual group sex parties, which means that attendees may identify as gay or lesbian or bisexual or hetero or transgendered, but are generally comfortable and happy to play side-by-side with people whose desires may be entirely different than their own."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d7586a3-6736-39e2-b08b-27f05a6dcbdd",
                                        "entry_id": "c3d90f71-9850-3d6f-aee7-3bf1e13fd1de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the psychological theory of pansexualism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pansexual",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d0ff7cf-3496-3329-bdc1-19f26d5b263f",
                                        "entry_id": "84306dcc-7d85-351a-b9f8-6dca90219026",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who is attracted to all types of people regardless of gender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e0da81d-93bb-4084-aa8d-ccbb2bfba0a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                        "target_lang_word": "omnisexual",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omnisexual",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f814e6d5-356f-3fb9-81a7-5d6b452c1470",
                                        "entry_id": "9f771063-8f55-3603-9570-417aa0b40b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being attracted to all genders (sometimes distinguished from pansexual by saying omnisexual attraction may still take account of gender or prefer particular genders)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fcf2ee4-140a-45e9-ba3c-4ff29a5e5728",
                                                "sense_id": "f814e6d5-356f-3fb9-81a7-5d6b452c1470",
                                                "text": "This omnisexual libertine who shuttles between his whore and his catamite (with equally regular visits to his tailor) has no classical prototype since aggressive bisexuality was completely acceptable as ‘masculine’ behaviour in ancient Greek society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "391d1b9f-4ec1-468e-85c8-505cdb4e1d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "f814e6d5-356f-3fb9-81a7-5d6b452c1470",
                                                "text": "There was something in this that made our relationship more than homosexual, and more than heterosexual. Perhaps it could be called an omnisexual relationship."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bcb15dd-683b-4e81-9d4f-3aa3b7583fe3",
                                                "sense_id": "f814e6d5-356f-3fb9-81a7-5d6b452c1470",
                                                "text": "In short, all readers can share, consciously and/or unconsciously, Whitman’s omnisexual vision—omnisexual in the all-encompassing sense of embracing auto-, homo-, and heteroerotic impulses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5b76168-f4f7-4e4a-91fd-b9afcb138ae3",
                                                "sense_id": "f814e6d5-356f-3fb9-81a7-5d6b452c1470",
                                                "text": "These Oedipal tensions are mirrored by a structural conflict between the [new Doctor Who] series’ tacit multiculturalism—captured by omnisexual Captain Jack Harkness, who exemplifies an exogamous future humankind that goes to the stars to “dance” with every species they meet—and the drive to reunite the nuclear family […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d38a51c-063a-3e2e-9ea1-e1b231abbe97",
                                        "entry_id": "9f771063-8f55-3603-9570-417aa0b40b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Androgynous, exhibiting traits of all sexes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10177992-1ccd-41d1-bf34-b1949fb473ce",
                                                "sense_id": "8d38a51c-063a-3e2e-9ea1-e1b231abbe97",
                                                "text": "Psyche’s participation in the archetypical patterns of heroic action logically implies that heroism itself is an asexual or omnisexual archetype."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9399d5f-9d41-4b9a-b4a8-b1eef3a2cc7a",
                                                "sense_id": "8d38a51c-063a-3e2e-9ea1-e1b231abbe97",
                                                "text": "Historically, sameness sexism marks the disappearance of conditions in which goddess religions flourished: prepatriarchal conditions in which men imagined women as awesome, omnipotent birth-givers, omnisexual creatures with both big breasts and penises."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "154b15f6-bec9-302a-bc01-88b0f75ac7ef",
                                        "entry_id": "9f771063-8f55-3603-9570-417aa0b40b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or exhibiting sexuality everywhere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec1b1189-6e33-4c0d-86b4-94970da3dfe0",
                                                "sense_id": "154b15f6-bec9-302a-bc01-88b0f75ac7ef",
                                                "text": "Both Queen Victoria and Sigmund Freud have, however, become common adjectives in our time, one describing the Dark Ages of sexual repression, the other an omnisexual world in which everything has sexual significance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f34538a3-0a92-45c7-bdcb-0cb49f098f4d",
                                                "sense_id": "154b15f6-bec9-302a-bc01-88b0f75ac7ef",
                                                "text": "To be a virgin in high school wasn't, even in the omnisexual milieu of the Pioneer Valley, such a social black spot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4007cdb8-5b55-470b-ba5b-0d783d4e3edc",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc1a386f-d148-3253-9a28-4656e9dd7d02",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f7b2936-84aa-3404-9b20-b5ab2f74036f",
                        "target_lang_word": "omni-sexual",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
